  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Lifted Cannabis Maine is a medical cannabis dispensary operating in Houlton, the seat of Aroostook County in far northern Maine. The operator's site explicitly states "Medical Card Required, No Adult Use/Recreational — Grown for smokers, By smokers." The focus is on serving the medical cannabis patient base in Aroostook County, a region that has historically had limited access to licensed dispensaries compared to southern and central Maine.</p>
    <p>Owner Zachary Waite has been an active voice in Houlton's cannabis ordinance debate. In August 2024, he addressed the Houlton Town Council advocating for changes to the town's medical marijuana ordinance to allow caregiver retail stores. His testimony highlighted that the state-level framework had changed but the town's local ordinance had not kept pace — a common pattern in small Maine municipalities with limited cannabis retail experience.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>Lifted Cannabis primarily serves northern Maine:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Houlton</strong> (operator's home base) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Presque Isle</strong> — 60 mi north on I-95</li>
      <li><strong>Caribou</strong> — 80 mi north</li>
      <li><strong>Fort Fairfield</strong> — 20 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Limestone</strong> — 30 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Van Buren</strong> — 45 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Madawaska</strong> — 60 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Houlton International Airport / NB border</strong> — 5 min</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Cross-border patients from New Brunswick (Woodstock, Perth-Andover, Grand Falls) can purchase medical cannabis in Maine with proper documentation. The Houlton border is one of the more traveled in northern Maine.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Product Standard and Pricing</h2>
    <p>Per the operator's public site (liftedmaine.com):</p>
    <ul>
